WEBVTT

00:15.724 --> 00:17.934
RESIDENT PLAYBOOK

00:19.436 --> 00:20.603
Are things going well in EM?

00:22.731 --> 00:24.274
Were you with OS last rotation?

00:24.357 --> 00:25.191
How was that?

00:25.275 --> 00:26.735
It wasn't great there either.

00:26.818 --> 00:28.653
The second-year residents are so scary.

00:29.612 --> 00:31.489
So they're the problem in OS.

00:32.407 --> 00:34.367
In OB-GYN,
the first-years are the problem.

00:34.451 --> 00:35.952
Why? What's wrong with them?

00:38.621 --> 00:39.456
They're all

00:41.166 --> 00:42.000
a bit unwell.

00:42.667 --> 00:43.585
Breathe.

00:44.085 --> 00:46.296
One has body temperature
that's way too low.

00:46.921 --> 00:48.173
She has hypothermia for sure.

00:48.256 --> 00:49.716
Ma'am, please push.

00:50.800 --> 00:52.177
I think I'm going to die.

00:53.178 --> 00:54.679
You're not there yet. Push.

00:55.764 --> 00:58.892
Then shouldn't they crank up
the heat in the labor room?

00:58.975 --> 01:00.060
Good.

01:00.143 --> 01:01.728
-No way.
-Push one more time.

01:01.811 --> 01:02.812
There's another one with…

01:02.896 --> 01:03.772
Okay, ma'am!

01:03.855 --> 01:05.023
-…a high fever.
-Breathe in!

01:05.607 --> 01:07.567
There you go! Very good!

01:07.650 --> 01:09.986
One, two, three!

01:15.408 --> 01:16.326
One more time!

01:16.409 --> 01:18.870
One, two, three!

01:22.332 --> 01:24.042
Ma'am, push!

01:25.085 --> 01:28.254
And there's one whose BP is way too high.
She has high blood pressure.

01:28.922 --> 01:29.756
One more time.

01:32.592 --> 01:34.636
Good! That's awesome!

01:35.220 --> 01:37.055
-That was so good!
-And the last one…

01:37.138 --> 01:38.723
Her vitals can't be measured.

01:39.224 --> 01:40.600
She can't be diagnosed.

01:40.683 --> 01:42.560
Doctor, it hurts so much.

01:43.728 --> 01:44.813
Ma'am, breathe.

01:46.231 --> 01:47.774
Ma'am, are you seeing white?

01:48.316 --> 01:49.150
No.

01:50.026 --> 01:51.653
Then we're not there yet.

01:51.736 --> 01:53.279
Call me when you see white.

01:53.947 --> 01:55.406
It's been confirmed she's not human.

01:55.490 --> 01:56.658
What on earth is she saying?

01:58.993 --> 02:01.621
My next rotation
is OB-GYN next month. I'm screwed.

02:03.206 --> 02:07.252
But in some ways, they seem okay.

02:08.253 --> 02:10.004
What? You said they were all unwell.

02:10.088 --> 02:11.798
The residents are weird,

02:11.881 --> 02:13.758
but when you see babies being born,

02:14.342 --> 02:15.218
it's really nice.

02:16.136 --> 02:19.931
The mothers and patients are all nice.

02:20.014 --> 02:21.349
It's hard work,

02:23.309 --> 02:24.144
but it's nice.

02:27.772 --> 02:29.315
-What in the world?
-You scared me.

02:31.484 --> 02:33.611
The alarm went off
because you were saying nonsense.

02:34.320 --> 02:35.155
My medication alarm.

02:35.238 --> 02:37.407
I have high blood pressure too.
It's time for my meds.

02:39.951 --> 02:40.869
Let's go.

02:40.952 --> 02:41.786
All right.

02:48.543 --> 02:49.711
They're interns, right?

02:50.587 --> 02:51.754
Who else are they? Fellows?

02:52.922 --> 02:53.923
Right.

02:55.258 --> 02:56.843
Doesn't the intern Tak Gi-on

02:57.719 --> 02:59.470
seem interested in OB-GYN?

02:59.554 --> 03:01.723
You're already preparing
to recruit interns?

03:01.806 --> 03:04.100
What do you mean "already"?
It's July. We're late.

03:05.351 --> 03:07.562
Our current first-years
didn't turn out well at all.

03:07.645 --> 03:10.481
If they're duds next year too,
we're all screwed.

03:11.482 --> 03:12.942
You better get it together.

03:13.026 --> 03:13.860
Right.

03:14.777 --> 03:15.612
Yes, ma'am.

03:17.363 --> 03:18.239
Let's go.

03:19.198 --> 03:20.033
Yes, ma'am.

03:27.582 --> 03:30.793
RESIDENT PLAYBOOK

03:32.378 --> 03:35.298
EPISODE 7

03:47.101 --> 03:49.312
I got chewed out by Prof. Seo
for not suturing well.

03:49.395 --> 03:51.189
She said to watch you and practice.

03:52.023 --> 03:53.191
-Nam-kyung.
-What?

03:53.274 --> 03:54.192
You too, right?

03:54.275 --> 03:55.860
No, I wasn't scolded.

03:56.486 --> 03:58.071
It was just a bit of nagging.

04:03.243 --> 04:04.744
You always pretended to slack off.

04:04.827 --> 04:05.954
You must've practiced a lot.

04:06.037 --> 04:06.996
I didn't.

04:07.747 --> 04:09.123
For abdominal fascia sutures,

04:09.207 --> 04:12.877
Prof. Kong says
to suture tightly to prevent hernias.

04:12.961 --> 04:15.296
But Prof. Seo will yell at you
for suturing too tightly,

04:15.380 --> 04:16.965
because it restricts blood flow.

04:17.799 --> 04:19.092
But what's the difference?

04:19.175 --> 04:20.510
She did it Prof. Seo's way.

04:21.469 --> 04:22.303
Really?

04:22.387 --> 04:23.221
You didn't know?

04:23.888 --> 04:26.057
No. I just did whatever they'd tell me.

04:27.350 --> 04:28.184
Is she a genius?

04:28.268 --> 04:29.727
Genius, my foot.

04:29.811 --> 04:31.938
They say if you're not smart,
you'll end up toiling.

04:32.522 --> 04:35.441
While toiling away,
she probably just got lucky.

04:35.525 --> 04:36.526
Yi-young is smart.

04:37.026 --> 04:38.945
You said she was
the top student in high school.

04:39.028 --> 04:40.154
I had the best grades.

04:40.238 --> 04:41.948
She did the best on mock exams.

04:42.031 --> 04:43.616
We were rivals for three years.

04:43.700 --> 04:45.743
None of that matters.

04:45.827 --> 04:47.745
Being the top student
in high school is useless.

04:47.829 --> 04:49.914
I'm broke and hungry now.

04:50.540 --> 04:51.791
I'm a total bum.

04:54.252 --> 04:55.378
You bought another bag?

04:55.962 --> 04:56.796
This?

04:57.797 --> 04:59.549
I took out a 12-month installment plan.

04:59.632 --> 05:01.718
This was the last one
in the country in this color.

05:01.801 --> 05:02.635
So what could I do?

05:03.219 --> 05:04.304
I had to buy it.

05:04.387 --> 05:05.221
Isn't it pretty?

05:05.305 --> 05:06.139
Well…

05:06.806 --> 05:07.890
it's not my taste.

05:08.516 --> 05:09.809
It's like a bag for older women.

05:10.685 --> 05:12.103
You don't know what's trendy.

05:12.729 --> 05:14.605
Don't you know
what the "old-money look" is?

05:14.689 --> 05:16.858
-Where would you even take that?
-Plenty of places.

05:16.941 --> 05:18.067
To and from work.

05:18.151 --> 05:19.402
The hospital. My home.

05:19.986 --> 05:20.987
She has a lot to go to.

05:21.070 --> 05:23.406
She has to go on dates
and see her boyfriend.

05:23.489 --> 05:25.033
I told you several times we broke up.

05:25.116 --> 05:27.076
You said it was just a fight.

05:27.160 --> 05:28.077
I'm off.

05:29.329 --> 05:31.247
We broke up! It's over!

05:31.831 --> 05:33.791
Even if he calls again,
I won't ever pick up.

05:33.875 --> 05:36.127
Even if he breaks down
and begs me to meet,

05:36.711 --> 05:38.838
there's nothing I can do
since I won't ever see him.

05:39.505 --> 05:40.506
This again?

05:40.590 --> 05:43.426
Just tell me if it was a fight
or a breakup once you decide.

05:43.509 --> 05:45.553
I told you it's been decided.

05:46.929 --> 05:48.431
Geez, I said it's really over.

05:51.851 --> 05:55.021
Doctor, the ER patient's results
are ready.

05:58.274 --> 06:01.027
Gi-dong, call me
when you're not mad anymore.

06:01.110 --> 06:02.361
I'll be waiting.

06:05.239 --> 06:06.074
It's the ER.

06:07.533 --> 06:08.534
I'm off.

06:31.766 --> 06:33.017
My phone!

06:47.323 --> 06:48.366
That's what I said.

06:49.742 --> 06:50.785
Hello.

06:50.868 --> 06:51.828
Hey, it's…

06:53.496 --> 06:54.956
Dr. Pyo Nam-kyung.

06:55.039 --> 06:55.873
Where are you going?

06:55.957 --> 06:58.751
The ER. I'm going to see
a patient with our intern.

06:58.835 --> 07:00.086
The one on his GYN rotation…

07:01.504 --> 07:03.005
Our intern…

07:03.798 --> 07:05.800
Dr. Tak Gi-on. Right?

07:05.883 --> 07:06.717
Yes.

07:07.218 --> 07:08.219
Go on.

07:08.302 --> 07:09.720
Have a good day.

07:11.222 --> 07:12.098
Oh, right.

07:12.974 --> 07:15.768
I heard the interns on OB-GYN rotation

07:15.852 --> 07:18.187
say that you're their favorite.

07:18.729 --> 07:19.564
Me?

07:19.647 --> 07:21.441
Especially that doctor…

07:22.984 --> 07:24.152
You know.

07:24.235 --> 07:26.446
Who? I don't know.

07:27.447 --> 07:29.782
The intern who was with us in April.

07:30.575 --> 07:35.663
They said you were so friendly
and such a kind teacher.

07:36.247 --> 07:37.248
That's what I heard.

07:38.249 --> 07:40.293
I didn't do much though.

07:40.376 --> 07:44.130
That's great. I was worried
no one would apply to OB-GYN next year,

07:44.213 --> 07:46.549
but we can just count on Dr. Pyo.

07:46.632 --> 07:47.967
Me?

07:48.050 --> 07:51.345
A lot of interns choose their departments
based on the senior residents.

07:53.473 --> 07:56.934
And without junior residents,
the seniors suffer the most.

07:57.018 --> 08:00.521
So try your best to persuade the interns.

08:01.647 --> 08:04.150
Yes, ma'am. I will.

08:05.151 --> 08:06.027
Good luck.

08:06.861 --> 08:07.695
Thank you.

08:09.989 --> 08:11.157
I'll get going.

08:16.704 --> 08:18.998
I hope she can just bring Dr. Tak over.

08:19.081 --> 08:22.418
But are you really sure
that intern's good though?

08:22.502 --> 08:23.836
I told you he is.

08:23.920 --> 08:26.172
He's perceptive and skilled.

08:26.255 --> 08:28.007
He's the perfect fit for OB-GYN.

08:28.841 --> 08:31.594
It's not cholangitis, so don't worry.

08:32.220 --> 08:34.931
Judging from the cough I have,
it's just a cold.

08:36.307 --> 08:38.643
I know the doctors here. Don't worry.

08:39.685 --> 08:41.646
-May I come in?
-Yes.

08:41.729 --> 08:42.897
The doctor's here.

08:42.980 --> 08:44.815
I'll call you back. Bye.

08:46.817 --> 08:48.069
Are you Ms. Lee Ik-sun?

08:48.152 --> 08:49.362
Yes.

08:49.445 --> 08:50.905
We're going to run an EKG.

08:50.988 --> 08:51.822
Sorry?

08:53.199 --> 08:55.326
I didn't do this last time.

08:55.409 --> 08:56.702
Why am I doing it this time?

08:58.996 --> 09:01.499
It seems metastasis is causing
your current symptoms.

09:01.582 --> 09:03.793
There may be a heart issue,
so they want us to check.

09:04.502 --> 09:05.336
Metastasis?

09:05.419 --> 09:06.629
Yes.

09:06.712 --> 09:08.714
Then, that means…

09:09.882 --> 09:12.051
You're saying it's cancer?

09:15.012 --> 09:18.724
Have your cough and chest tightness
been worse recently?

09:19.308 --> 09:20.393
Yes, coughing…

09:21.686 --> 09:22.728
I had a cough.

09:22.812 --> 09:25.523
My chest did seem a little tight too.

09:27.692 --> 09:29.193
And you've had major surgery before?

09:30.027 --> 09:31.028
Yes, that's right.

09:31.612 --> 09:33.322
I'm sure you had a hard time then as well.

09:35.866 --> 09:38.452
Is it really bad?

09:40.580 --> 09:41.831
Sorry, excuse me.

09:43.207 --> 09:44.625
Hi. I'm not done yet.

09:46.794 --> 09:49.755
I said don't worry.
I'll call you right after I'm done.

09:51.048 --> 09:51.966
Okay, bye.

09:56.887 --> 10:00.683
I'm finally off my meds now,
and I thought I was getting better.

10:02.184 --> 10:04.270
But this is so unfair.

10:06.188 --> 10:07.023
What's going on?

10:07.607 --> 10:08.858
Hey, come on in.

10:11.235 --> 10:12.320
What, are you really sick?

10:14.697 --> 10:15.906
Is something wrong?

10:17.074 --> 10:17.908
Well…

10:17.992 --> 10:19.118
Are the results in?

10:20.036 --> 10:21.787
Could I see the CT results?

10:21.871 --> 10:23.080
Well…

10:23.164 --> 10:24.707
Dr. Tak, what are you doing here?

10:24.790 --> 10:25.625
Dr. Pyo.

10:26.459 --> 10:27.960
I was going to do an EKG,

10:29.545 --> 10:31.380
but the patient became bit startled.

10:35.301 --> 10:36.761
Ms. Lee Ik-sun?

10:36.844 --> 10:37.970
Yes.

10:40.681 --> 10:43.267
Ms. Lee Ik-sun, age 89?

10:44.894 --> 10:45.728
Eighty…

10:48.648 --> 10:49.899
Which department are you with?

10:50.483 --> 10:51.817
GS? GI?

10:52.526 --> 10:53.611
OB-GYN.

10:56.072 --> 10:58.324
I'm very sorry.

10:58.407 --> 11:00.534
I think our intern has the wrong patient.

11:00.618 --> 11:01.702
I'm really sorry.

11:02.953 --> 11:05.247
Isn't checking patient identity
the most basic thing?

11:06.123 --> 11:08.626
It's a mistake you can't make
no matter how busy you are.

11:09.293 --> 11:11.212
I'm sorry. It won't happen again.

11:12.963 --> 11:13.881
Goodbye.

11:13.964 --> 11:15.716
-I'm sorry.
-I'm sorry.

11:18.344 --> 11:21.263
Why did you do that? Geez, come on.

11:21.347 --> 11:22.348
I'm sorry.

11:25.851 --> 11:26.977
Captain Ahn.

11:28.104 --> 11:30.314
Your juniors have become
way too undisciplined.

11:32.775 --> 11:34.110
I apologize, Major.

11:34.193 --> 11:36.028
I was so shocked. My nose is running.

11:36.987 --> 11:38.572
I need a tissue.

11:42.743 --> 11:43.661
Wait…

11:43.744 --> 11:45.788
Are you going to do the dove thing?

11:47.998 --> 11:50.543
I'm going to blow my nose, okay?
It's running.

11:50.626 --> 11:51.877
I was so surprised.

11:51.961 --> 11:54.505
Also, I've become old.

11:55.256 --> 11:57.007
My fingers are too stiff
to do the dove now.

11:57.091 --> 11:58.384
But you work out a lot.

11:58.467 --> 11:59.301
I do.

11:59.927 --> 12:02.054
That's why I'm hanging on like this.

12:02.138 --> 12:03.347
Goodness.

12:03.431 --> 12:04.932
What about you?

12:05.850 --> 12:07.852
You look like you don't work out at all.

12:09.353 --> 12:10.521
What's wrong with how I look?

12:11.439 --> 12:13.441
I look totally fine.

12:13.524 --> 12:15.317
I'm like Gen Z in mind and body.

12:17.403 --> 12:18.654
That's so embarrassing. Fine.

12:18.737 --> 12:22.324
Then I'll treat you
to dinner tonight as the elder.

12:22.408 --> 12:24.160
What do you want, Gen Z? Pasta?

12:24.243 --> 12:27.538
No. I saw a place on my way here.
Brick-oven pizza.

12:28.664 --> 12:29.665
I need to eat rice.

12:30.249 --> 12:31.417
Koreans need rice.

12:32.460 --> 12:35.087
There's a great
beef bone soup place nearby.

12:35.171 --> 12:36.005
We can go there.

12:36.088 --> 12:39.341
Hey, what kind of Gen Z eats
beef bone soup? Have some pasta.

12:39.425 --> 12:40.843
-Hey, Gen Z.
-Just a moment, ma'am.

12:42.261 --> 12:43.762
Yes, I'll be right there.

12:45.514 --> 12:46.765
Hey, Gen Z. Pasta.

12:46.849 --> 12:49.685
Kids these days like beef bone soup.

12:50.936 --> 12:53.564
How have you become so old already?

12:53.647 --> 12:55.566
-Good luck with treatment. See you later.
-Okay.

12:58.694 --> 13:01.322
Who wouldn't be scared
if you suddenly say it's metastasized?

13:01.989 --> 13:04.700
You should have double-checked
before saying that.

13:05.326 --> 13:06.160
I'm sorry.

13:06.952 --> 13:09.497
Things got busy all of a sudden,
and I lost focus.

13:10.247 --> 13:13.584
From now on,
always check the patient's name and age.

13:13.667 --> 13:15.753
Ask for their identification too, okay?

13:16.337 --> 13:18.130
Yes. I'm sorry.

13:18.881 --> 13:19.965
For goodness' sake.

13:22.176 --> 13:23.219
And thank you.

13:24.595 --> 13:27.348
The other first-year resident
always gets mad.

13:28.557 --> 13:29.683
They tell me to get lost.

13:30.768 --> 13:32.019
Who would say that?

13:33.062 --> 13:34.271
Dr. Oh.

13:35.814 --> 13:38.150
But you explained what I did wrong

13:38.234 --> 13:40.236
and how I should fix it.

13:42.029 --> 13:42.863
It's so nice.

13:44.240 --> 13:47.243
You can't just say anything
no matter how angry you are.

13:47.326 --> 13:49.036
Gosh, I can't even speak casually.

13:50.037 --> 13:53.123
Even if you're a junior,
I have to be respectful.

13:57.461 --> 13:59.463
Yes, this is
Jongno Yulje Medical Center ER.

13:59.547 --> 14:01.882
All beds are full right now.
Please try another hospital.

14:01.966 --> 14:04.677
-We've been waiting forever.
-Sorry, we'll be with you soon.

14:04.760 --> 14:06.387
When will that be?

14:06.470 --> 14:08.055
I came to the ER for a consult.

14:08.722 --> 14:09.723
Yes, I'll be right there.

14:11.058 --> 14:14.520
Hello, I was called to look at a mass
on a CT for abdominal pain.

14:15.396 --> 14:17.898
-Please go over there to E.
-Okay.

14:21.485 --> 14:24.989
The CT shows a 3 cm ovarian cyst.

14:25.823 --> 14:28.242
Yes, that was already there.

14:29.034 --> 14:31.996
Abdominal pain isn't common
for something that small.

14:32.746 --> 14:33.581
Just a moment.

14:35.124 --> 14:37.793
-Does that hurt?
-No, not there.

14:38.377 --> 14:39.879
You're sure the pain isn't down here?

14:42.089 --> 14:44.425
If it's from the cyst,
it should hurt here.

14:47.261 --> 14:48.137
Then how about here?

14:54.476 --> 14:56.020
Doctor? Knock-knock.

14:56.103 --> 14:57.187
I'm busy right now.

14:58.022 --> 14:59.940
Doctor, I looked at the patient.

15:00.566 --> 15:02.484
The pain isn't where the cyst is.

15:02.568 --> 15:04.862
She has upper abdominal pain
and indigestion.

15:05.779 --> 15:07.364
So why did you call us?

15:07.448 --> 15:09.617
Before, she said it hurt all over.

15:09.700 --> 15:14.872
You see, not all abdominal pain
in women is related to OB-GYN.

15:14.955 --> 15:17.458
We couldn't confirm cholecystitis
from the CT scan.

15:17.541 --> 15:20.836
We thought it could've been
ovarian cyst torsion, so we called OB-GYN.

15:20.920 --> 15:22.671
I also called Gastroenterology.

15:23.547 --> 15:27.760
Well, torsion from a 3 cm cyst

15:27.843 --> 15:28.844
is not very common.

15:28.928 --> 15:30.596
I guess that's true.

15:30.679 --> 15:32.681
But it doesn't hurt to check.

15:32.765 --> 15:34.934
Last week,
we were called for an appendicitis.

15:35.017 --> 15:37.645
That patient had a history
of ovarian surgery.

15:37.728 --> 15:39.438
The week before that,
it was for gastritis.

15:39.521 --> 15:41.607
She had severe menstrual cramps.

15:41.690 --> 15:43.859
All she needed were painkillers,
but you still called.

15:44.485 --> 15:46.153
You said to call you promptly last time.

15:47.571 --> 15:48.405
Sorry?

15:49.114 --> 15:51.241
Last week,
you scolded us for calling too late

15:51.325 --> 15:52.826
with all the OB-GYN patients waiting.

15:53.410 --> 15:55.704
The week before that,
you said we couldn't diagnose

15:55.788 --> 15:57.122
since we had no OB-GYN knowledge.

15:57.706 --> 15:59.667
You told us to call
instead of wasting time.

16:01.043 --> 16:02.378
That's not what we meant.

16:03.545 --> 16:06.298
It's just we've received
especially a lot of calls lately

16:06.924 --> 16:08.842
when it's not OB-GYN-related.

16:08.926 --> 16:10.177
Then should we not call you?

16:12.221 --> 16:13.097
Really?

16:14.682 --> 16:15.516
No.

16:15.599 --> 16:16.600
See?

16:17.184 --> 16:18.686
I'll call again if there's a patient.

16:19.311 --> 16:20.396
Thanks.

16:25.693 --> 16:28.529
Dr. Park Moo-kang from Pediatrics?
It's Kim Sa-bi from OB-GYN.

16:28.612 --> 16:30.030
It's about Ms. Yoo Hong-seon.

16:30.114 --> 16:31.740
Is the baby coming? Should I come now?

16:31.824 --> 16:34.910
No. Progress is slow,
so I think the baby will come tomorrow.

16:34.994 --> 16:35.911
Really?

16:35.995 --> 16:38.038
So can I go eat then? Can I?

16:38.122 --> 16:39.123
I'm really going to go.

16:39.206 --> 16:40.958
I think that's for you to decide.

16:41.041 --> 16:44.336
Tomorrow morning,
I'll call you again with an update.

16:44.420 --> 16:45.421
Okay, bye.

16:58.642 --> 17:00.019
Doctor, Ms. Yoo's baby is coming!

17:00.102 --> 17:01.228
-Please come now!
-What?

17:01.812 --> 17:03.105
You said it wasn't coming today.

17:03.188 --> 17:05.524
The baby's coming now!
Its heart rate is falling. Hurry!

17:05.607 --> 17:07.443
You said I could eat.

17:08.402 --> 17:09.445
I'm coming.

17:13.157 --> 17:14.575
Geez, OB!

17:30.466 --> 17:32.051
You did so well.

17:32.760 --> 17:35.137
DELIVERY ROOM

17:35.220 --> 17:36.221
Very good.

17:38.182 --> 17:40.934
Doctor, is the baby okay?
Is it breathing well?

17:41.018 --> 17:44.396
Yes, you said the baby's heart rate
was falling, but it's perfectly fine.

17:44.480 --> 17:45.564
Doctor,

17:46.398 --> 17:48.525
if the baby's okay,
then why are you angry?

17:49.943 --> 17:51.653
Isn't that a good thing?

17:51.737 --> 17:52.821
Why is he mad?

17:53.405 --> 17:54.448
No, I wasn't angry…

17:58.577 --> 18:00.162
Yes, this is Dr. Park from Pediatrics.

18:02.206 --> 18:05.042
Ms. Park Sol's baby in the NICU?
I'll be right there. I'm sorry.

18:05.793 --> 18:09.046
I mean, how many times are you going
to call Anesthesiology today?

18:10.297 --> 18:12.633
For local anesthesia,
we have to use a thick needle,

18:12.716 --> 18:15.135
so you may feel some discomfort.

18:15.219 --> 18:16.220
Okay.

18:22.851 --> 18:25.145
You've heard of "pain-free heaven," right?

18:25.229 --> 18:26.855
You'll be there soon. Just hold on.

18:30.818 --> 18:32.611
It won't hurt much
once the epidural goes in.

18:32.694 --> 18:33.946
Please relax.

18:41.495 --> 18:44.248
Still, isn't calling
every 30 minutes excessive?

18:44.331 --> 18:47.251
Can't you do it all at once?
This my fifth time here today.

18:47.334 --> 18:48.669
I'm sorry.

18:48.752 --> 18:51.547
I'm serious. A liver transplant,
peritonitis, and cerebral hemorrhage.

18:51.630 --> 18:53.298
Three surgeries
opened at the same time.

18:53.382 --> 18:55.259
Each operating room is in chaos.

18:55.342 --> 18:56.260
Us too.

18:57.219 --> 19:01.140
The mothers screamed in the delivery room
that they were in pain every 30 minutes.

19:01.223 --> 19:02.641
Their husbands complained.

19:03.142 --> 19:04.268
It was total chaos.

19:04.351 --> 19:05.602
That is OB's problem.

19:05.686 --> 19:07.729
We're not some rapid-response unit.

19:09.148 --> 19:10.649
Excuse me, Doctor!

19:13.777 --> 19:14.653
Doctor!

19:15.154 --> 19:16.280
Doctor!

19:16.363 --> 19:19.741
The epidural from an hour ago didn't work.
She needs it again. Now!

19:22.286 --> 19:23.287
Can you

19:24.830 --> 19:28.458
keep the cancer a secret?

19:29.042 --> 19:32.504
If my mother knows it's cancer,
she'll never have the surgery.

19:32.588 --> 19:34.339
But now,

19:34.882 --> 19:38.010
I think it would be better
for the treatment if she knew.

19:38.093 --> 19:40.179
Well…

19:42.639 --> 19:45.392
This year, both her friend and my aunt

19:46.393 --> 19:49.563
passed away
after a tough battle with cancer.

19:50.230 --> 19:51.648
After that,

19:51.732 --> 19:54.234
she said even surgery
wouldn't help with cancer

19:55.485 --> 19:57.946
and that she'd never spend time
suffering in a hospital.

19:59.114 --> 20:00.115
This time,

20:00.824 --> 20:03.994
I barely managed to bring her here
by telling her it was a cyst.

20:05.871 --> 20:08.916
To do this surgery, this is the only way.

20:08.999 --> 20:12.377
Afterwards, I'll take
full responsibility and tell her.

20:18.300 --> 20:20.469
The mung bean pancake lady
at Pyeongnam Market.

20:20.552 --> 20:21.386
Sir?

20:22.429 --> 20:23.764
Just now… Don't you know?

20:24.556 --> 20:25.891
She says money should be spent

20:25.974 --> 20:29.269
on kids who have full lives ahead of them,
not old people like her.

20:29.353 --> 20:32.105
So she donates
100 million won yearly to Pediatrics.

20:32.189 --> 20:33.690
She was on You Quiz on the Block too.

20:35.400 --> 20:37.694
So that's why the hospital director
came to say hello?

20:37.778 --> 20:38.862
Yeah.

20:38.946 --> 20:41.114
She does so many good things.

20:42.324 --> 20:44.368
But… Wait.

20:46.453 --> 20:48.956
Think of this
as a small thank you for that,

20:50.040 --> 20:53.126
and let's be careful about what we say.

20:53.794 --> 20:55.295
I know it's a bit of a hassle.

20:56.088 --> 20:57.339
-Yes, sir.
-Yes, sir.

20:58.715 --> 21:00.634
Is everyone getting off work?
How about dinner?

21:00.717 --> 21:02.135
-I have plans.
-Sounds good, sir.

21:08.308 --> 21:11.061
It's all right. Relax.
Don't worry about it.

21:11.687 --> 21:12.521
Okay.

21:12.604 --> 21:14.439
-Let's go.
-Okay.

21:14.523 --> 21:17.359
Enjoy your dinner.

21:18.652 --> 21:19.861
Thank you.

21:19.945 --> 21:21.822
You too, Professor.

21:21.905 --> 21:22.823
I will.

21:29.288 --> 21:30.289
Fresh ribs.

21:32.791 --> 21:33.875
Marinated ribs.

21:35.877 --> 21:36.878
Whole pork belly!

21:38.755 --> 21:39.965
Eat up.

21:40.048 --> 21:42.384
It was a pain arranging a night
when you all were free.

21:42.467 --> 21:44.052
-Thank you!
-Thank you!

21:49.141 --> 21:51.935
Dr. Ku, you're close
with Dr. Park Jun-suk from EM, right?

21:52.019 --> 21:52.936
Not particularly.

21:53.645 --> 21:54.896
Can't you have a word with him?

21:54.980 --> 21:57.649
EM's been stressing me out so much
that I might go bald.

21:58.608 --> 21:59.443
I mean,

22:00.152 --> 22:03.572
if a female patient's stomach hurts,
they call us without checking properly.

22:04.364 --> 22:06.074
Why call OB-GYN for cholecystitis?

22:07.826 --> 22:09.244
Maybe they needed you to check.

22:11.455 --> 22:13.915
It's not that.
They're like, "We called you."

22:13.999 --> 22:15.834
"Someone hurry and take this patient."

22:15.917 --> 22:18.920
Geez. That's why people mock them
and say they're a call center.

22:19.004 --> 22:20.505
Scold Pediatrics too.

22:20.589 --> 22:22.341
Why would I do that?

22:22.424 --> 22:26.011
They get mad if I call them
either too soon or too late.

22:26.094 --> 22:27.846
They get really upset
over even tiny things.

22:27.929 --> 22:30.724
Pediatrics is about as generous
as the size of their patients.

22:30.807 --> 22:32.392
There's a lot who aren't like that.

22:32.476 --> 22:33.643
There can't be a lot.

22:33.727 --> 22:35.395
Their department barely has anyone.

22:36.688 --> 22:38.065
Don't forget about Anesthesiology.

22:38.148 --> 22:40.233
They stand near the patient's head
and act superior.

22:40.317 --> 22:41.568
They're so arrogant.

22:42.152 --> 22:43.695
They think they own the OR.

22:45.030 --> 22:46.448
What about OB-GYN?

22:47.324 --> 22:50.118
We always thoughtlessly
push our way into the OR.

22:50.202 --> 22:52.579
We use babies as threats
to boss people around.

22:52.662 --> 22:54.831
That's why everyone mocks us
as the "thugs of Yulje."

22:54.915 --> 22:56.333
People don't like us either.

22:56.416 --> 22:58.960
And they don't need anything from us.

22:59.044 --> 23:01.296
If we fight, it only hurts us
since we always need help.

23:01.379 --> 23:03.965
So try to get along, okay?

23:09.805 --> 23:11.890
Tonight, let's just eat
and not talk about work.

23:12.474 --> 23:13.767
-Yes, sir!
-Yes, sir!

23:19.856 --> 23:20.941
I'm so full.

23:21.900 --> 23:23.151
Gosh, I'm stuffed!

23:24.319 --> 23:26.530
-Thank you for the meal.
-Thank you for the meal.

23:26.613 --> 23:27.697
See you tomorrow.

23:27.781 --> 23:29.157
-Good night!
-See you tomorrow!

23:29.241 --> 23:30.408
-Good night.
-Take care, sir.

23:35.789 --> 23:36.957
-See you.
-Bye.

23:37.040 --> 23:37.874
Bye.

23:47.217 --> 23:48.635
Weren't you going back to work?

23:49.219 --> 23:50.345
No, I'm going home.

23:51.388 --> 23:52.681
But why did you go that way?

23:54.182 --> 23:55.016
What?

23:57.310 --> 23:59.354
I got lost and thought home was that way.

24:04.943 --> 24:07.279
Were you worried
the others would get the wrong idea?

24:08.238 --> 24:10.073
They'd just assume
we're going the same way.

24:10.866 --> 24:13.243
They're not as nosy as you think.

24:14.369 --> 24:16.580
You're the one who told me
to not say anything.

24:17.789 --> 24:18.665
I did?

24:20.208 --> 24:22.586
But why take this street
and not the main one?

24:23.170 --> 24:24.462
This is the fastest way.

24:25.589 --> 24:27.257
But it's so dark.

24:28.133 --> 24:29.676
And empty.

24:30.552 --> 24:32.345
It seems a bit dangerous to walk alone.

24:41.021 --> 24:44.274
I mean, what if you
come across some weirdo?

24:48.486 --> 24:49.779
I'll punch them in the face.

24:50.363 --> 24:51.698
And smack them in the ear.

24:54.993 --> 24:56.578
So you are a thug.

24:56.661 --> 24:57.704
You really are.

25:05.545 --> 25:08.006
Did you box during high school
or something?

25:08.632 --> 25:09.549
What do you mean?

25:10.300 --> 25:11.801
I heard you're a good puncher.

25:12.928 --> 25:14.179
What are you talking about?

25:21.102 --> 25:23.021
-Is it that good?
-Yeah.

25:23.939 --> 25:25.607
This place has the best crabs.

25:25.690 --> 25:27.067
I'll buy much more next time.

25:27.150 --> 25:29.319
I went too late,
and they only had two left.

25:30.528 --> 25:32.489
I need to replenish my stamina.

25:32.572 --> 25:35.951
When I had the egg retrieval last time,
I realized how weak I was.

25:39.120 --> 25:42.374
Getting the shots
while having a cold was really tough.

25:43.166 --> 25:47.379
This time, I'll eat well,
get healthier, and then--

25:47.462 --> 25:49.089
You said that was the last time.

25:49.714 --> 25:50.674
You said you were done.

25:50.757 --> 25:51.758
When did I say that?

25:52.384 --> 25:55.303
I said I'd see how many embryos grow
and only do that much.

25:55.887 --> 25:57.764
Having zero embryos
wasn't part of the plan.

25:57.847 --> 25:58.848
It doesn't count.

25:58.932 --> 26:00.350
But you cried so much.

26:00.433 --> 26:03.061
I did? When? No, I didn't.

26:05.563 --> 26:07.190
I think it'll go well this time.

26:07.899 --> 26:09.192
I can feel it.

26:12.404 --> 26:13.488
They're home already?

26:14.656 --> 26:15.740
Clear the table!

26:15.824 --> 26:17.367
The crab fiend's here. Oh, no!

26:21.496 --> 26:23.248
-I'm home.
-Me too.

26:23.331 --> 26:24.499
You came home together.

26:24.582 --> 26:26.209
Yes, we had dinner together.

26:28.962 --> 26:31.131
Not just us two.
With the other first-years too.

26:32.215 --> 26:33.174
We didn't say anything.

26:33.258 --> 26:35.385
We were curious
if you had something good without us.

26:35.468 --> 26:36.428
We had barbecue.

26:36.511 --> 26:37.679
I'll go wash up.

26:37.762 --> 26:39.014
-Okay.
-All right.

26:48.773 --> 26:49.649
Hey, Joo-young.

26:58.033 --> 26:59.617
What is this?

27:00.827 --> 27:01.661
What do you mean?

27:06.124 --> 27:07.625
That's all you're eating?

27:07.709 --> 27:08.543
What?

27:11.171 --> 27:12.255
It's seaweed.

27:12.339 --> 27:15.675
This is all I need to eat all of my rice.

27:16.343 --> 27:18.136
You need to eat better.

27:19.346 --> 27:20.930
Seung-won, can you wake me up tomorrow?

27:21.014 --> 27:23.099
Okay, Yi-young. Good night.

27:24.184 --> 27:25.352
What am I doing?

27:27.270 --> 27:28.104
She didn't catch us.

27:58.093 --> 27:59.427
How did you know about the crabs?

28:01.888 --> 28:03.973
Didn't you see the soy sauce drop
by the seaweed?

28:04.057 --> 28:07.394
It's lighter than brewed soy sauce
and more aromatic than soup soy sauce.

28:07.477 --> 28:09.854
Then what else could it be?
It's marinated raw crabs.

28:13.441 --> 28:15.777
My brother bought it for your sister.

28:16.403 --> 28:17.987
It's from her favorite place.

28:18.613 --> 28:20.115
He must've stood in line for it.

28:21.241 --> 28:23.535
That's why I'm only eating the legs.

28:25.370 --> 28:27.163
Is it even worth eating that?

28:27.247 --> 28:29.249
I was full anyway. Just a taste…

28:29.999 --> 28:31.000
I'm just having a taste.

28:40.468 --> 28:41.386
Why are you up though?

28:42.929 --> 28:44.013
I had some papers to read.

28:45.098 --> 28:47.308
Why are you reading
so many of those boring things?

28:47.392 --> 28:49.352
You stayed up reading
the last two nights too.

28:49.436 --> 28:51.146
I napped in the resident's lounge.

28:55.150 --> 28:56.735
I bet there's nothing in there.

28:59.154 --> 29:01.156
Stop eating. I'll buy you some next time.

29:04.367 --> 29:05.243
Really?

29:08.288 --> 29:10.165
Just me without Joo-young?

29:11.708 --> 29:12.584
Okay.

29:15.962 --> 29:16.880
When?

29:17.672 --> 29:18.715
How about this Friday?

29:19.966 --> 29:20.800
Okay.

29:20.884 --> 29:22.010
Nice.

29:22.093 --> 29:22.927
No, I can't.

29:24.262 --> 29:25.096
Why not?

29:25.638 --> 29:27.390
I have somewhere to go. I forgot.

29:27.474 --> 29:28.808
Damn it.

29:46.618 --> 29:48.620
You go on leave tomorrow. Right, Dr. Ku?

29:49.120 --> 29:50.038
Was it for three days?

29:50.121 --> 29:51.080
Yes, Professor.

29:51.164 --> 29:52.749
You should've taken more days off.

29:52.832 --> 29:54.375
You've been so busy this whole time.

29:54.459 --> 29:56.669
And you must've had
a hard time with that paper.

29:56.753 --> 29:57.754
Sorry? What do you mean?

29:58.421 --> 29:59.422
I mean get some rest.

29:59.506 --> 30:01.466
I'll make sure no one calls you.

30:02.050 --> 30:03.593
Okay. Thank you.

30:08.181 --> 30:11.184
Do-won, are you really off
starting tomorrow?

30:11.267 --> 30:12.101
Yes, Professor.

30:12.185 --> 30:15.647
Then, can you help me out
a lot today before you go?

30:15.730 --> 30:16.648
Sure, Professor.

30:16.731 --> 30:19.859
Then, could you review my paper,
the summer symposium presentation,

30:19.943 --> 30:23.154
and Prof. Im's retirement ceremony plans?

30:25.490 --> 30:28.076
I just can't trust the juniors with them.

30:28.701 --> 30:29.661
Yes, of course.

30:29.744 --> 30:33.665
And I have two surgeries today.

30:33.748 --> 30:35.208
I'll be assisting you on both.

30:36.960 --> 30:40.088
I swear I won't call you on your vacation.

30:40.171 --> 30:41.422
-Thanks.
-Sure.

30:42.131 --> 30:45.051
Is she telling you
to go on vacation or not?

31:00.984 --> 31:03.236
I heard our chief resident's
going on holiday.

31:03.319 --> 31:04.612
Yes, Professor.

31:04.696 --> 31:06.656
Right. Are you busy today?

31:07.615 --> 31:08.658
No, I'm not.

31:09.742 --> 31:11.411
-No, right?
-No.

31:14.163 --> 31:15.707
JONGNO YULJE MEDICAL CENTER

31:16.332 --> 31:19.210
Did Prof. Jo scold you a lot
over the surgery records?

31:19.294 --> 31:20.128
Yes.

31:21.254 --> 31:23.548
My goodness. Look.

31:23.631 --> 31:26.968
If it's benign, always add
the uterus weight in the surgery record.

31:27.802 --> 31:29.178
And when making the diagram,

31:29.262 --> 31:31.931
mark the direction the uterus
was removed in with an arrow.

31:36.561 --> 31:39.981
And remind him one more time tonight
about tomorrow's first surgery.

31:40.064 --> 31:42.150
There's a frozen section
for tomorrow's last surgery,

31:42.233 --> 31:43.943
so remember to book with Pathology.

31:44.027 --> 31:45.194
Okay, I will.

31:46.654 --> 31:48.698
Are you coming in to assist tomorrow?

31:48.781 --> 31:50.700
No, I won't be here tomorrow.
I'll be on leave.

31:51.534 --> 31:52.368
Oh, right!

31:53.661 --> 31:54.621
Where are you going?

31:55.455 --> 31:57.373
Taiwan. I'm hopping on a plane.

31:58.750 --> 32:00.460
What's wrong with this consent form?

32:00.543 --> 32:01.836
Oh, that?

32:01.920 --> 32:04.797
That's for the pancake lady.
We made the font larger.

32:04.881 --> 32:07.175
The Pyeongnam Market
mung bean pancake lady?

32:08.217 --> 32:10.470
The font on the form was too small.

32:11.054 --> 32:12.221
It'd be hard for her to read.

32:14.933 --> 32:17.060
Her son asked us to keep it a secret.

32:17.143 --> 32:18.978
She doesn't know she has cancer.

32:19.646 --> 32:22.273
I also checked to make sure
cancer wasn't mentioned.

32:24.025 --> 32:26.945
I mean, I won't let it slip.

32:27.779 --> 32:29.113
But I'm worried about the intern.

32:29.197 --> 32:30.949
He's quite the troublemaker.

32:31.032 --> 32:33.201
Dr. Tak Gi-on, right? How is he doing?

32:34.702 --> 32:36.537
I'm teaching him well.

32:37.830 --> 32:41.167
He really trusts and relies on me.

32:44.212 --> 32:45.171
Dr. Pyo?

32:45.755 --> 32:46.589
Yes?

32:47.131 --> 32:49.133
I think you should come and look.

32:56.891 --> 32:58.142
Just a moment.

32:58.226 --> 32:59.102
Okay.

33:01.104 --> 33:02.021
A moment, please?

33:10.822 --> 33:11.948
Dr. Tak?

33:12.740 --> 33:15.743
Are you drawing stars on her belly?
You can't tape her like that.

33:17.078 --> 33:17.954
Sorry?

33:19.163 --> 33:20.039
Then, how…

33:20.123 --> 33:22.000
Put a long strip over the affected area

33:22.083 --> 33:24.752
from top to bottom
to help the skin close better.

33:26.629 --> 33:27.588
I'm sorry.

33:28.423 --> 33:30.883
I was worried
water would get in while showering.

33:30.967 --> 33:34.262
I mean, you're struggling to remove
the Hemovac and PICC,

33:34.345 --> 33:35.847
so I'm doing them all for you.

33:37.849 --> 33:39.684
That's more work for me.

33:40.184 --> 33:42.437
You should at least figure out
how to tape on your own.

33:43.146 --> 33:44.105
I'm sorry.

33:44.731 --> 33:47.400
Could you do better next time?

33:50.319 --> 33:51.195
Okay.

33:55.450 --> 33:56.451
-Ma'am?
-Yes?

33:56.534 --> 33:59.662
I'm afraid we'll need to reapply the tape.

34:00.371 --> 34:01.372
Again?

34:02.498 --> 34:03.541
Yes.

34:04.167 --> 34:06.836
Be careful to not let
water in when showering.

34:06.919 --> 34:08.755
On your next outpatient visit,

34:08.838 --> 34:11.466
we'll check how they're healing
and redress them.

34:12.050 --> 34:12.925
Okay.

34:13.468 --> 34:15.011
Hello.

34:15.094 --> 34:17.221
You said you're leaving
early tomorrow morning,

34:17.305 --> 34:19.891
so we've prepared everything
for an early discharge.

34:19.974 --> 34:20.808
Thank you.

34:21.726 --> 34:24.937
But, Professor, is this okay?

34:25.897 --> 34:28.107
I feel like
they might fall off right away.

34:28.191 --> 34:30.318
Don't worry, ma'am. I taped them well.

34:30.401 --> 34:34.238
Well, that male doctor
did it very thoroughly earlier.

34:34.322 --> 34:37.658
But the retaping she did
doesn't feel as secure.

34:38.367 --> 34:41.537
Then, let me take a look at it.

34:43.998 --> 34:45.666
Yes, it's fine.

34:45.750 --> 34:46.959
They've been taped well.

34:47.043 --> 34:48.211
Really?

34:51.756 --> 34:52.590
That's incredible.

34:55.051 --> 34:59.305
I wonder how our male doctor did it
if it was better than this.

34:59.388 --> 35:02.850
He did it so thoroughly
that even a drop of water wouldn't get in.

35:03.601 --> 35:05.436
I don't know why she did it again.

35:06.020 --> 35:07.522
No, it wasn't like that--

35:07.605 --> 35:09.148
It's all right. Don't worry.

35:09.232 --> 35:10.858
There's no need to be humble right now.

35:11.442 --> 35:12.318
Sir?

35:13.861 --> 35:14.695
Yeah.

35:16.447 --> 35:17.448
Thank you.

35:18.491 --> 35:19.492
I'm so curious.

35:25.998 --> 35:26.833
Yi-young, what's up?

35:26.916 --> 35:27.834
You scared me.

35:28.793 --> 35:30.711
I'm withdrawing some cash. You?

35:31.838 --> 35:32.797
I had a savings plan.

35:32.880 --> 35:33.965
-Savings?
-Yeah.

35:34.048 --> 35:35.424
It matured, so I'm closing it.

35:35.508 --> 35:36.342
Matured?

35:37.844 --> 35:39.303
Some people really do pull that off.

35:40.179 --> 35:41.764
You could suddenly need a lot of cash.

35:41.848 --> 35:43.599
You could move or go travel,

35:43.683 --> 35:44.517
so we need to save.

35:45.601 --> 35:47.645
I know that. I just can't do it.

35:47.728 --> 35:49.355
You don't have a savings plan?

35:49.438 --> 35:50.314
I've never tried.

35:51.023 --> 35:52.608
Some people really do live recklessly.

35:54.402 --> 35:55.820
But I do one thing similar to that.

35:55.903 --> 35:57.113
What?

35:59.198 --> 36:00.032
The lottery.

36:00.116 --> 36:01.617
There's a prime spot near my house.

36:01.701 --> 36:02.994
Eight winners came from there.

36:09.834 --> 36:11.252
-We've got a patient.
-We've got a patient.

36:12.378 --> 36:13.254
-Yes, Doctor.
-Yes.

36:13.337 --> 36:14.172
I'll be right there.

36:14.255 --> 36:15.756
-I'm on my way!
-No!

36:15.840 --> 36:19.135
Ten centimeters to the left
and five to the right would do it.

36:19.760 --> 36:20.761
Doctor?

36:21.554 --> 36:23.055
This isn't a parking lot.

36:23.681 --> 36:26.767
If you made a little space,
you could fit one more in here.

36:26.851 --> 36:28.728
There's no one to care for it.

36:28.811 --> 36:30.813
Shoving in a bassinet
won't solve anything.

36:30.897 --> 36:33.941
We can't shove the baby back in,
so we have to push this in.

36:34.984 --> 36:37.236
We're completely full right now.

36:37.320 --> 36:39.155
Remember the three sets
of twins yesterday?

36:39.238 --> 36:41.741
I remember. At two, five,
and one in the morning.

36:41.824 --> 36:42.742
That's right.

36:42.825 --> 36:44.577
That's three deliveries for OB.

36:44.660 --> 36:46.996
For us, it's six more, okay?

36:47.997 --> 36:50.625
It's not that we don't want to take it.
We just can't.

36:50.708 --> 36:53.085
Goodness, are you hungry?

36:53.169 --> 36:54.670
Wait just a second.

36:56.214 --> 36:57.173
How precious.

36:57.256 --> 36:59.091
We're short-staffed.

36:59.175 --> 37:00.635
Don't you watch the news?

37:00.718 --> 37:02.803
Pediatrics has no applicants
or first-year residents.

37:02.887 --> 37:04.263
And people are slowly quitting.

37:04.347 --> 37:07.308
So I've done three straight shifts.
I've been up for almost 36 hours.

37:08.059 --> 37:10.186
I do feel for you about that.

37:10.269 --> 37:13.522
But why do you always
share Pediatrics' stats with me?

37:14.815 --> 37:16.984
It's to tell you no.

37:17.777 --> 37:18.778
It's a no.

37:18.861 --> 37:19.820
It's a no for me too.

37:20.404 --> 37:22.865
Prof. Seo said
the mother can't be transferred.

37:23.449 --> 37:26.661
Then are you going to feed the newborns
and rock them to sleep…

37:28.496 --> 37:30.998
Are you going feed and put them to sleep?

37:31.582 --> 37:33.334
Is it a yes if I do?

37:34.543 --> 37:36.295
If I feed them, can we add a bassinet?

37:36.379 --> 37:37.213
Now look here.

37:40.424 --> 37:42.009
Yes, this is Dr. Park from Pediatrics.

37:43.177 --> 37:45.471
Hui-yul is throwing up?
I'll be right there.

37:46.555 --> 37:48.307
I clearly said no, okay?

37:48.391 --> 37:50.101
If you put a bassinet in, I swear…

38:05.366 --> 38:06.659
Yi-young, I got a spot!

38:06.742 --> 38:07.576
Okay.

38:13.874 --> 38:15.626
-There are no rooms.
-Right.

38:15.710 --> 38:17.378
I know, but we need one.

38:17.461 --> 38:19.130
-It's an emergency.
-I'm sure it is.

38:19.714 --> 38:22.341
If I give you one,
we have to delay all the other surgeries.

38:22.425 --> 38:23.718
Thanks to OB-GYN last night,

38:23.801 --> 38:26.178
other departments chewed us out
for their delayed surgeries.

38:26.262 --> 38:27.847
Please, just this once.

38:27.930 --> 38:29.390
There's an urgent C-section.

38:29.473 --> 38:30.683
You saw when you came here.

38:30.766 --> 38:32.977
There are no Anesthesiology staff
or rooms left.

38:33.060 --> 38:34.562
The surgery is impossible.

38:36.439 --> 38:39.150
So you're saying
we absolutely can't do it?

38:39.233 --> 38:40.318
Yes.

38:40.401 --> 38:42.987
Then I'll tell the mother
we can't do it due to Anesthesiology

38:43.070 --> 38:45.072
and she needs to transfer hospitals.

38:46.032 --> 38:47.033
What?

38:47.116 --> 38:48.826
Are you threatening me right now?

38:48.909 --> 38:54.248
Or should I tell her to hold the baby in
until Anesthesiology can give us a room?

38:55.333 --> 38:57.460
You are so mean. You really are.

38:57.543 --> 38:59.628
I can't afford to worry
about anyone else right now.

38:59.712 --> 39:01.255
And no other hospitals can take her.

39:09.555 --> 39:10.431
Hey, Sang-hyeon.

39:11.098 --> 39:13.100
Can you push back the OS surgery?

39:13.809 --> 39:16.270
Just beg them again.
Theirs isn't an emergency.

39:17.104 --> 39:19.190
Yeah. Just one hour.

39:20.524 --> 39:21.942
Who do you think? OB-GYN.

39:26.197 --> 39:27.031
Thank you!

39:32.495 --> 39:34.497
Professor, I got an OR.

39:34.580 --> 39:35.748
I'll bring her down.

39:40.002 --> 39:42.630
Doctor, I got a call
about a pregnant patient.

39:42.713 --> 39:44.673
-She's over there. I'll be there soon.
-Okay.

39:47.468 --> 39:48.969
-Call Neurosurgery.
-Okay.

39:49.595 --> 39:50.763
I'll disinfect your wound.

39:50.846 --> 39:51.764
It might sting.

39:55.726 --> 39:56.769
Her fever's high.

39:58.354 --> 40:01.357
Doctor, are the CBC and CRP results in?

40:04.860 --> 40:05.986
We didn't run the tests yet.

40:06.904 --> 40:07.780
How about the UA?

40:08.656 --> 40:10.366
We were going to do that,

40:10.449 --> 40:13.285
but she couldn't produce
any urine, so not yet.

40:14.829 --> 40:18.541
So you called me
even though you didn't run any tests?

40:22.670 --> 40:24.171
I'm sorry, Dr. Um.

40:24.255 --> 40:26.257
But could we run the tests

40:26.340 --> 40:28.217
after transferring her
to the delivery room?

40:29.051 --> 40:32.763
When we're busy,
other OB-GYN doctors would do that for us.

40:35.558 --> 40:37.184
We have a lot of patients today.

40:37.268 --> 40:39.353
All the beds are full. Look.

40:45.151 --> 40:46.444
Our delivery room's the same.

40:47.778 --> 40:49.405
The labor room's full too.

40:49.488 --> 40:51.282
It's pure chaos.

40:51.866 --> 40:52.950
I see.

40:54.994 --> 40:56.787
But couldn't you take her just this once?

41:00.499 --> 41:01.584
Could we?

41:08.132 --> 41:10.676
I'm sorry, we're really busy too.

41:11.260 --> 41:14.430
Please run the urinalysis
and blood tests for CBC, CRP, PCT,

41:14.513 --> 41:16.891
electro, OPTP, BUN, and creatinine.

41:16.974 --> 41:18.684
And if you do a sonogram too,

41:18.767 --> 41:21.770
we'll make her transfer
swift and accurate.

41:22.354 --> 41:23.272
Oh, right.

41:23.856 --> 41:24.773
All right.

41:25.399 --> 41:27.234
Give me a call
when the tests are complete.

41:28.527 --> 41:29.361
Thank you.

41:33.782 --> 41:35.034
He's a lot sharper now.

41:36.285 --> 41:37.536
That was a fail.

41:37.620 --> 41:39.622
He wasn't always like that.

41:41.457 --> 41:43.459
-Nurse, could we run the blood work?
-Okay.

41:44.376 --> 41:45.669
-It looks great!
-It looks great!

41:48.422 --> 41:50.049
Let's eat.

41:52.176 --> 41:54.261
-Let's dig in.
-Let's eat!

42:02.394 --> 42:04.605
I had no energy to debone.
Thank God it's boneless.

42:04.688 --> 42:08.359
A patient gave it to us for letting her
safely have her baby here.

42:10.194 --> 42:11.028
Right!

42:11.111 --> 42:12.988
You got to have chicken when celebrating.

42:13.072 --> 42:15.658
But why are all of you so happy?

42:15.741 --> 42:18.035
It's 11:30 p.m., and we're stuck here.

42:18.619 --> 42:20.162
I really gave it to the EM team.

42:20.829 --> 42:22.456
I destroyed them with cold, hard facts.

42:22.540 --> 42:23.457
Hey, good job.

42:24.124 --> 42:26.085
They think we're fools
because we hold back.

42:26.168 --> 42:27.294
Exactly.

42:27.378 --> 42:28.671
Being nice gets you nothing.

42:28.754 --> 42:30.714
You'll just go mad. No!

42:31.382 --> 42:33.425
Don't put up with it! Watch out!

42:33.509 --> 42:37.012
Right, being patient three times
is too much.

42:37.096 --> 42:37.930
No more.

42:38.681 --> 42:39.807
What is this?

42:39.890 --> 42:41.976
Why are you three
suddenly on the same page?

42:42.601 --> 42:45.145
Are you all now,
"United we stand! Together as one!"

42:45.229 --> 42:46.272
And things like that?

42:47.231 --> 42:48.315
Are you?

42:49.733 --> 42:50.568
Hey, guys.

42:51.151 --> 42:52.736
Check your patients' operability.

42:52.820 --> 42:55.447
And Ms. Ahn Ho-jin in MFICU
will likely deliver soon,

42:55.531 --> 42:57.241
so watch for labor signs.

42:57.950 --> 42:58.867
-Okay.
-Okay.

42:58.951 --> 43:00.035
You're still here though?

43:00.119 --> 43:01.537
Isn't your flight tomorrow morning?

43:03.080 --> 43:05.374
I'm just about to grab my things
and leave. Bye.

43:09.336 --> 43:11.797
Don't call me and ask, "Where are you?"

43:11.880 --> 43:13.841
"I'm sorry. Could I ask a question?"

43:13.924 --> 43:15.009
Especially you, Jae-il.

43:15.092 --> 43:16.510
Don't. I won't stand for it.

43:16.594 --> 43:19.763
Come on. You're gone for three days,
not three months.

43:19.847 --> 43:21.265
Who do you think I am?

43:21.849 --> 43:23.726
We can do things on our own now too.

43:23.809 --> 43:25.311
Don't you worry.

43:25.394 --> 43:26.520
Have fun.

43:26.604 --> 43:28.355
A small gift will suffice.

43:30.316 --> 43:32.276
Okay, see you next week.

43:32.359 --> 43:33.611
-Safe travels!
-Bye!

43:38.198 --> 43:39.825
JONGNO YULJE MEDICAL CENTER

43:41.035 --> 43:44.079
Anytime we ask something,
they say to ask the chief resident.

43:44.163 --> 43:45.664
It was my mistake,

43:46.957 --> 43:49.668
but they blamed the chief for not checking
and said to bring him.

43:51.211 --> 43:53.422
How many times can we say
Ku Do-won's not here?

43:54.798 --> 43:56.216
What's shocking is

43:57.843 --> 43:59.595
he hasn't even been gone for a day.

44:08.812 --> 44:10.522
Everyone's looking for the chief resident.

44:10.606 --> 44:11.774
But why is he looking for me?

44:11.857 --> 44:12.733
Who?

44:12.816 --> 44:13.817
The intern.

44:14.318 --> 44:17.863
Leaving him alone makes me anxious,
but being next to him makes me angry.

44:20.741 --> 44:23.452
Dr. Ku must have felt the same way.

44:27.039 --> 44:29.041
I should go before he screws up. Bye.

44:29.124 --> 44:35.506
OB-GYN 4TH-YEAR RESIDENT LOUNGE

44:45.015 --> 44:46.850
This is different from that one.

44:47.476 --> 44:49.311
It's a consent form
for epidural anesthesia.

44:49.395 --> 44:51.647
It'll let us use medicine
so you won't feel pain.

44:51.730 --> 44:52.981
That's what it's about.

44:53.065 --> 44:54.400
If you look here…

44:54.483 --> 44:57.778
I'm just removing a small cyst.
Is it that painful?

45:01.156 --> 45:02.574
It's different for everyone.

45:03.200 --> 45:05.536
But given your age,
it may be more painful.

45:05.619 --> 45:07.704
So we'd like to prepare this in advance.

45:07.788 --> 45:10.416
How long does it take to remove the cyst?

45:11.291 --> 45:14.962
Including the prep and anesthesia,
about an hour and a half.

45:16.713 --> 45:18.424
That's longer than I thought.

45:18.507 --> 45:21.593
Yes, cancer surgeries
usually take a while.

45:22.219 --> 45:24.596
But compared to other cancer surgeries,
it's pretty short.

45:25.681 --> 45:26.515
Really?

45:30.310 --> 45:31.478
Cancer surgery?

45:32.354 --> 45:33.188
Yes.

45:34.398 --> 45:35.274
Who has cancer?

45:36.358 --> 45:37.234
Me?

45:42.030 --> 45:44.783
If it's cancer surgery,
you're saying I have cancer?

45:45.492 --> 45:46.785
Not a cyst but cancer?

45:50.706 --> 45:51.707
Yes, it's…

45:52.332 --> 45:53.917
It's cancer.

46:00.132 --> 46:01.049
So,

46:02.176 --> 46:05.304
you had all known
from the beginning except for me?

46:05.387 --> 46:06.680
That I had cancer?

46:06.763 --> 46:09.975
How can a hospital
lie to its own patient?

46:10.058 --> 46:11.685
I asked them to.

46:12.352 --> 46:14.980
Because I knew you'd refuse surgery.

46:18.317 --> 46:19.485
You should have the surgery.

46:21.111 --> 46:23.489
The imaging suggests
it's at a very early stage,

46:23.572 --> 46:26.867
and the prognosis appears to be good.

46:26.950 --> 46:29.203
And a laparoscopic surgery

46:30.037 --> 46:31.330
doesn't leave much of a scar.

46:31.413 --> 46:33.332
So recovery will be quick too.

46:33.415 --> 46:36.293
They told my sister she'd live too.

46:37.085 --> 46:39.963
But she ended up suffering
in the hospital and died.

46:41.089 --> 46:44.134
Gosh, I don't want
to waste time like that.

46:44.885 --> 46:47.679
I guess they're saying I'm old now,
and it's my time to go.

46:47.763 --> 46:50.349
So it's okay to die just for being old?

46:51.225 --> 46:52.476
Says who?

46:52.559 --> 46:54.728
The law? Does it say that in books?

46:54.811 --> 46:57.189
Let's have the surgery, Mom.

46:57.981 --> 47:02.027
Let's make more pancakes
to let more children get surgery.

47:02.110 --> 47:05.572
It's not for you but for the children.

47:07.199 --> 47:09.409
You don't want that either? No?

47:10.327 --> 47:11.662
Mom.

47:12.204 --> 47:13.664
Your son is right.

47:14.331 --> 47:15.624
Please have the surgery, ma'am.

47:15.707 --> 47:17.334
Please.

47:18.126 --> 47:19.336
It's all my fault.

47:20.045 --> 47:22.047
I'm sorry, ma'am. Please.

47:29.763 --> 47:31.932
I never wanted surgery.

47:32.683 --> 47:34.518
And I'm upset you all lied to me,

47:34.601 --> 47:36.728
so I was going to leave.

47:44.820 --> 47:47.489
But I'll think it over for this doctor.

47:51.368 --> 47:52.578
Because I'm grateful.

47:53.453 --> 47:55.372
But it was really nothing--

47:55.455 --> 47:57.332
For being honest with me.

47:59.501 --> 48:00.627
If it weren't for you,

48:00.711 --> 48:04.381
I would've never known about my illness
or what would happen to me

48:04.464 --> 48:06.216
before being dragged into surgery.

48:06.717 --> 48:09.553
What kind of fool would I have become?

48:12.764 --> 48:14.558
Thank you for telling me.

48:16.059 --> 48:18.353
You're the only one I can trust.

48:18.437 --> 48:22.399
I'm an ignorant old woman,
so it must have been easy to fool me.

48:24.234 --> 48:25.277
We apologize.

48:26.153 --> 48:27.237
I'm sorry.

48:28.113 --> 48:31.700
If I do go through with surgery,
will you be there?

48:37.080 --> 48:39.166
Yes. I'll be there, ma'am.

48:45.339 --> 48:47.132
-Okay, we'll see you for surgery.
-Yes.

48:47.215 --> 48:48.133
But,

48:49.343 --> 48:50.636
this surgical consent form…

48:50.719 --> 48:52.679
Why is the font like that?

48:53.597 --> 48:57.476
I enlarged the font for her
so it would be easier to read.

48:58.560 --> 49:00.062
Has she read it?

49:00.145 --> 49:01.980
My mother can't read.

49:02.064 --> 49:03.023
Excuse me?

49:03.106 --> 49:04.941
I think I told you before.

49:05.567 --> 49:06.943
But you just gave it and left.

49:08.695 --> 49:12.407
So my mother can just sign here, right?

49:14.451 --> 49:16.870
That was a copy for your reference.

49:16.953 --> 49:21.875
Before she signs, we'll make sure
to read it for her and explain everything.

49:22.542 --> 49:24.252
I see. Thank you.

49:28.131 --> 49:29.216
I eat it at home too.

49:29.299 --> 49:31.218
-I see.
-Yes.

49:31.301 --> 49:32.719
Fortune favors those who are lucky.

49:32.803 --> 49:34.763
Everything just goes well for them.

49:34.846 --> 49:36.098
Everything works out.

49:36.682 --> 49:40.018
Their timing couldn't be more perfect.
You know?

49:42.479 --> 49:43.355
Look.

49:43.438 --> 49:45.524
When you're on call, you get no calls.

49:45.607 --> 49:47.275
I had deliveries all night on my shift.

49:47.359 --> 49:49.319
Just go home if you're going to whine.

49:49.986 --> 49:52.197
If you're staying, take my shift.

49:52.823 --> 49:55.575
Because of emergency surgeries,
two of Prof. Ryu's were delayed.

49:55.659 --> 49:57.244
So I can't go!

49:57.828 --> 50:00.372
What a pain for those who are unlucky.

50:01.164 --> 50:02.040
You little…

50:08.422 --> 50:11.174
THURSDAY, JULY 20

50:25.522 --> 50:27.941
I'm going in for Ms. Jin's delivery.

50:28.024 --> 50:30.193
Keep your eye on the ward and ER.

50:30.277 --> 50:31.111
Yes, ma'am.

50:34.030 --> 50:35.198
Hello, OB-GYN.

50:38.452 --> 50:39.703
Yes, I'll be right there.

50:44.458 --> 50:47.210
She's not our patient, but came here
with her amniotic sac ruptured.

50:51.923 --> 50:53.133
Ma'am?

50:59.431 --> 51:01.141
So, your water broke.

51:05.228 --> 51:07.272
I don't speak English well

51:07.355 --> 51:09.191
or understand Korean.

51:09.274 --> 51:10.650
Am I okay?

51:10.734 --> 51:11.985
What on earth is she saying?

51:13.403 --> 51:15.655
Name? What's your name?

51:16.782 --> 51:20.786
Margarita Kalashnikova.

51:20.869 --> 51:22.454
-Margarita?
-Margarita.

51:22.537 --> 51:23.622
Margarita?

51:29.169 --> 51:30.045
Twins?

51:30.128 --> 51:31.671
No, I only saw one.

51:32.255 --> 51:33.381
She says it's twins.

51:33.465 --> 51:36.051
It's her second baby.
She had a C-section for her first.

51:43.141 --> 51:44.142
Thank you.

51:45.393 --> 51:47.771
Professor, a patient needs you in the ER.

51:47.854 --> 51:50.315
She's not our patient, but it's an ROM.

51:50.398 --> 51:52.275
The ultrasound shows
the baby is in breech.

51:52.359 --> 51:54.986
She's in active labor,
at Station 1.5, and effaced 50%.

51:55.070 --> 51:57.072
She'll need surgery,
so I'm calling in advance.

51:57.155 --> 51:58.949
Yeah, I'm in delivery,
but I'll be done soon.

51:59.950 --> 52:02.494
Prep for surgery.
I'll finish up and be there soon.

52:02.577 --> 52:03.411
Okay.

52:05.455 --> 52:06.331
Wait.

52:07.874 --> 52:09.125
The bleeding is severe.

52:18.343 --> 52:21.888
Our intern is assisting this evening

52:21.972 --> 52:23.265
to keep his promise.

52:23.348 --> 52:24.474
It's all right.

52:24.558 --> 52:27.894
He's kind to his patients,
and he's a good worker too.

52:27.978 --> 52:30.438
There's nothing but praise for him.

52:31.022 --> 52:33.108
Everyone's talking about Dr. Tak.

52:33.191 --> 52:34.025
My gosh.

52:34.109 --> 52:36.444
-You remembered his name, Professor?
-What?

52:37.070 --> 52:40.115
Yes. I etched it into my heart.

52:51.710 --> 52:54.337
Receiving praise as an intern

52:54.421 --> 52:56.214
is not an easy thing to do.

52:56.298 --> 52:57.841
Right? Doctor…

52:58.633 --> 52:59.801
Sir?

53:02.721 --> 53:05.265
Yes, of course.

53:05.348 --> 53:06.391
Thank you.

53:06.474 --> 53:08.643
In any case,
I hope I'll be seeing more of you

53:10.103 --> 53:11.396
for a long time.

53:11.479 --> 53:13.398
-Fan, please?
-Sir?

53:15.025 --> 53:15.859
Fan.

53:16.693 --> 53:17.694
Okay.

53:18.987 --> 53:21.406
I don't usually sweat this much.

53:22.115 --> 53:23.450
But it's so hot today.

53:26.202 --> 53:27.287
Wait.

53:27.829 --> 53:29.456
Not there.

53:29.539 --> 53:30.540
The wound.

53:31.124 --> 53:32.375
I applied glue on this wound.

53:33.710 --> 53:34.836
Oh, here!

53:34.920 --> 53:35.837
Right!

53:35.921 --> 53:38.340
-Wait, I need a minute.
-Here.

53:41.259 --> 53:45.138
Hold on. Were you always this hilarious?

53:46.097 --> 53:47.557
Look at this.

53:47.641 --> 53:49.517
OB-GYN is a lot of fun, right?

53:49.601 --> 53:51.102
Yes, it's hilarious.

53:53.104 --> 53:55.273
This really is a happy place, isn't it?

53:55.357 --> 53:57.108
Yes, it is.

54:00.779 --> 54:02.030
What's wrong with me?

54:02.113 --> 54:03.531
Why is it so hot today?

54:04.324 --> 54:06.201
Even though it was hot, nice work.

54:07.202 --> 54:09.329
-Good night, sir.
-Thank you.

54:13.917 --> 54:14.834
Dr. Tak.

54:17.295 --> 54:18.171
Are you laughing?

54:19.714 --> 54:21.007
You think it's funny?

54:26.763 --> 54:28.682
Why isn't Anesthesiology picking up?

54:32.102 --> 54:33.228
Doctor, it's OB-GYN.

54:33.311 --> 54:35.355
A patient needs emergency surgery.

54:35.438 --> 54:36.272
Did she fast?

54:36.856 --> 54:37.691
Fast…

54:42.028 --> 54:45.365
My hospital said there were no problems.

54:46.241 --> 54:47.701
Let me check and call you back.

54:47.784 --> 54:49.119
Could you prep the OR first…

54:51.579 --> 54:53.123
HAM DONG-HO

54:55.250 --> 54:56.710
I lost my phone,

54:56.793 --> 54:58.461
so I couldn't call.

54:58.545 --> 54:59.963
Have you seen my phone?

55:05.552 --> 55:07.137
The translation app.

55:09.681 --> 55:11.141
Does your stomach hurt?

55:17.439 --> 55:18.523
Damn it.

55:35.415 --> 55:37.751
What on earth? Why is it…

55:39.294 --> 55:40.670
When are we moving her?

55:40.754 --> 55:41.755
Now.

55:41.838 --> 55:42.756
What?

55:42.839 --> 55:44.591
Right now, the baby's foot…

55:44.674 --> 55:47.010
The baby's foot is out right now!

55:47.802 --> 55:49.721
-Nurse!
-Yes?

55:49.804 --> 55:51.431
Is something wrong with the baby?

55:51.514 --> 55:53.308
I'm not giving birth now, right?

55:58.980 --> 56:01.024
The baby's foot is out.
We have to move her.

56:01.107 --> 56:03.485
Contact her guardian now
and get the patient's history.

56:03.568 --> 56:04.402
Okay.

56:05.236 --> 56:07.489
-I'll call Anesthesiology.
-Thank you!

56:10.867 --> 56:12.327
I need an OR now.

56:12.410 --> 56:14.579
Just get me one now. It's OB-GYN.

56:14.662 --> 56:16.456
-Professor, you have to get here.
-Yeah, now!

56:16.539 --> 56:17.832
The baby's foot is out!

56:17.916 --> 56:21.669
There are vaginal and rectal tears,
so I'm suturing now.

56:22.212 --> 56:23.421
I think I'll be a while.

56:23.505 --> 56:24.631
What? Then, what do I do?

56:25.215 --> 56:26.466
No one else can come?

56:28.051 --> 56:30.762
Get the on-call GYN professor.
Tell them I asked. Hurry.

56:30.845 --> 56:33.014
That's Professor Ryu.
They're in emergency surgery.

56:33.098 --> 56:34.265
What do we do?

56:34.349 --> 56:36.184
Then you get ready.

56:36.267 --> 56:37.936
I'll have GS switch with me and go.

56:38.019 --> 56:39.687
Get ready, and if it's urgent,

56:39.771 --> 56:42.398
administer general anesthesia
and open her up when she's under.

56:42.482 --> 56:43.316
Okay.

56:43.900 --> 56:44.776
What?

56:44.859 --> 56:46.528
Open her up. I'll be right there.

56:47.028 --> 56:48.780
Can you call the on-call GS doctor?

56:49.489 --> 56:52.408
Check if Gi-sun
or Dr. Myeong can come too.

56:52.492 --> 56:53.326
Yes, ma'am.

56:54.702 --> 56:55.703
-Do we have an OR?
-Yes.

56:55.787 --> 56:57.789
The caregivers and nurses helped clean up.

56:57.872 --> 56:59.249
We pushed back an appendectomy.

56:59.332 --> 57:00.333
Thank you, Doctor.

57:00.416 --> 57:01.751
Any underlying conditions?

57:01.835 --> 57:03.211
-Any medications?
-We don't know.

57:03.294 --> 57:04.879
-Did she fast?
-I don't know.

57:04.963 --> 57:06.214
What's her weight?

57:07.006 --> 57:09.342
-Do you know her name?
-It's so long. I'm sorry.

57:14.222 --> 57:16.015
Isn't that Dr. Oh from OB-GYN?

57:16.099 --> 57:17.392
I think so.

57:17.934 --> 57:20.436
It must be really urgent
if they're going that fast.

57:21.980 --> 57:23.648
What is it now?

57:27.402 --> 57:30.155
Let me know when you're ready.
The anesthesia's been prepared.

57:38.079 --> 57:39.956
Dr. Oh, don't cry.

57:40.039 --> 57:42.041
If you shed tears,
you have to prep all over again.

57:42.125 --> 57:42.959
You know, right?

57:44.043 --> 57:45.211
Yes.

57:45.295 --> 57:46.504
If you have to pull it out--

57:46.588 --> 57:47.755
I can't.

57:47.839 --> 57:49.424
I understand you're scared, but…

57:49.507 --> 57:51.176
When did the foot come out?

57:51.259 --> 57:53.094
It was ten minutes ago.

57:53.178 --> 57:55.013
Patient's name is Margarita Kalashnikova.

57:55.680 --> 57:56.639
She's at 37 weeks,

57:56.723 --> 57:59.184
and she visited our ER
early in the pregnancy,

57:59.267 --> 58:00.894
but nothing was abnormal then.

58:00.977 --> 58:02.020
Her husband's on his way.

58:02.103 --> 58:03.813
He verbally gave his consent.

58:05.356 --> 58:06.357
Thanks.

58:06.441 --> 58:07.817
Find someone who can come.

58:09.444 --> 58:11.946
It's okay. Your husband is coming.

58:15.241 --> 58:16.951
I think we'll have to open her up.

58:17.035 --> 58:18.578
I can't. I've never done it before.

58:18.661 --> 58:21.164
It'll be dangerous
if blood doesn't flow to that leg.

58:22.123 --> 58:23.917
We're still looking for who can come.

58:24.000 --> 58:25.210
I'll assist for now.

58:25.293 --> 58:28.796
If the baby goes under too,
I can wake it, so take your time.

58:28.880 --> 58:30.548
I'll take good care of the baby, okay?

58:30.632 --> 58:32.675
Yes. I'll watch the mother carefully too.

58:32.759 --> 58:33.843
Calm down.

58:33.927 --> 58:36.888
We're all here.

58:40.433 --> 58:42.977
When Dr. Oh makes the incision,
pull the stomach down a bit.

58:43.645 --> 58:44.562
Okay.

58:46.981 --> 58:48.525
SURGERY IN PROGRESS

58:49.526 --> 58:50.568
She's under.

58:50.652 --> 58:51.736
Her vitals are good.

59:41.786 --> 59:42.620
Make the cut deeper.

59:48.960 --> 59:49.961
Dr. Ku!

01:00:09.647 --> 01:00:10.481
Get it together.

01:00:29.375 --> 01:00:30.418
Dr. Ham?

01:00:30.501 --> 01:00:31.836
Her vitals are okay.

01:00:31.919 --> 01:00:33.254
And--

01:00:33.338 --> 01:00:34.839
I contacted the NICU. Don't worry.

01:00:34.922 --> 01:00:35.923
Okay, thank you.

01:00:42.305 --> 01:00:43.139
Pull.

01:00:51.564 --> 01:00:52.440
Yes.

01:00:53.399 --> 01:00:55.443
I'm at the OB-GYN on-call room.

01:00:56.152 --> 01:00:57.236
No one's here.

01:01:00.198 --> 01:01:01.574
Yes, let me know.

01:01:02.158 --> 01:01:02.992
Okay, bye.

01:01:06.496 --> 01:01:08.581
Oh, dear. It seems like no one's here.

01:01:10.500 --> 01:01:11.876
Goodness.

01:01:11.959 --> 01:01:14.170
What do we do, Obstetrics?

01:01:19.717 --> 01:01:20.551
What on earth?

01:01:24.681 --> 01:01:26.099
This isn't Taiwan.

01:01:29.852 --> 01:01:31.729
There goes my plane ticket.

01:01:34.190 --> 01:01:35.316
It's an OB-GYN doctor.

01:01:38.653 --> 01:01:39.987
The baby's coming.

01:01:42.532 --> 01:01:44.534
It's 8:46 p.m., and it's a boy.

01:01:49.455 --> 01:01:50.707
Take the baby now.

01:01:52.834 --> 01:01:54.502
Wrap the sensor around
and clean the baby.

01:01:54.585 --> 01:01:55.461
Okay.

01:01:57.422 --> 01:01:58.673
Okay, cry for us.

01:01:59.549 --> 01:02:00.967
Come on, baby. Cry.

01:02:02.885 --> 01:02:04.595
Heart rate's under 100. I'll start PPV.

01:02:05.179 --> 01:02:06.389
-Oxygen, please.
-Okay.

01:02:07.598 --> 01:02:08.558
Yi-young, are you okay?

01:02:09.642 --> 01:02:10.560
-Professor!
-Professor!

01:02:10.643 --> 01:02:12.103
Did you get the baby out okay?

01:02:12.687 --> 01:02:13.563
Yes.

01:02:13.646 --> 01:02:15.231
-Are the mother's vitals okay?
-Yes.

01:02:15.314 --> 01:02:16.816
Nice work. Go rest.

01:02:16.899 --> 01:02:17.942
Yes, Professor.

01:02:18.943 --> 01:02:19.944
Are you okay?

01:02:20.027 --> 01:02:20.987
Let's switch, Yi-young.

01:02:21.070 --> 01:02:21.904
Okay.

01:02:22.905 --> 01:02:25.450
The baby's out,
and uterine contractions are good.

01:02:25.533 --> 01:02:26.951
Good job.

01:02:30.538 --> 01:02:31.372
Heart rate?

01:02:32.415 --> 01:02:33.750
It's under 100.

01:02:33.833 --> 01:02:35.168
-Stimulate him more.
-Okay.

01:02:35.251 --> 01:02:36.919
Come on, baby. Cry.

01:02:38.421 --> 01:02:39.505
Please.

01:03:16.626 --> 01:03:17.794
Is the baby okay?

01:03:17.877 --> 01:03:19.921
Yes, Apgar is 8,
and the saturation is fine.

01:03:20.004 --> 01:03:21.464
His pulse is also above 100.

01:03:22.006 --> 01:03:23.549
We'll move him to the NICU.

01:03:24.133 --> 01:03:25.802
Good work. Thank you.

01:03:26.969 --> 01:03:28.304
You did great too.

01:03:32.225 --> 01:03:33.059
Yi-young!

01:03:33.726 --> 01:03:34.727
Nice work.

01:03:34.811 --> 01:03:36.145
Really nice.

01:03:36.771 --> 01:03:37.814
Thank you.

01:03:38.397 --> 01:03:39.607
The mother's vitals are good.

01:03:40.274 --> 01:03:41.234
Dong-ho, good work.

01:03:41.317 --> 01:03:42.527
Thank you.

01:03:57.333 --> 01:03:58.668
Dr. Oh's been contaminated.

01:03:59.919 --> 01:04:03.339
Since you've been contaminated,
why don't you two leave and get some rest?

01:04:20.940 --> 01:04:23.860
OB-GYN

01:04:36.581 --> 01:04:38.875
Hey, Gi-dong!

01:04:41.043 --> 01:04:43.629
What? You're where?

01:04:50.720 --> 01:04:51.554
Nam-kyung.

01:04:57.101 --> 01:04:57.935
Gi-dong.

01:05:01.772 --> 01:05:02.899
Hello, Professor.

01:05:02.982 --> 01:05:05.359
The patient you called about
is now in the ER.

01:05:05.443 --> 01:05:07.570
The CT shows EDH
on the right temporal lobe,

01:05:07.653 --> 01:05:08.946
and it's a lot.

01:05:09.030 --> 01:05:12.408
Mental status is stupor.
Left motor function is grade 3.

01:05:12.491 --> 01:05:14.118
I'll move them to the OR now.

01:05:15.953 --> 01:05:16.787
Okay, bye.

01:05:20.249 --> 01:05:21.417
Hello, Doctor.

01:05:23.085 --> 01:05:24.670
OB-GYN, right?

01:05:24.754 --> 01:05:27.089
Yes, I'm first-year OB-GYN, Pyo Nam-kyung.

01:05:27.715 --> 01:05:30.843
I wanted to ask you something
about a patient.

01:05:30.927 --> 01:05:32.094
Yes?

01:05:32.178 --> 01:05:34.388
It's the one who fell down the stairs.

01:05:34.472 --> 01:05:35.514
Ms. Jo Suk-hui?

01:05:35.598 --> 01:05:38.100
Yes, I'd like to know her test results.

01:05:38.184 --> 01:05:39.644
Just a moment.

01:05:44.023 --> 01:05:48.152
The CT didn't show
any cerebral hemorrhage or skull fracture.

01:05:49.820 --> 01:05:53.908
But it was a big fall,
so a week's rest is needed,

01:05:53.991 --> 01:05:56.619
and she should come back
if she notices anything abnormal.

01:05:57.620 --> 01:05:59.372
Okay. Thank you.

01:05:59.455 --> 01:06:01.415
She's not a GYN patient, is she?

01:06:01.499 --> 01:06:02.500
Sorry?

01:06:02.583 --> 01:06:04.752
I don't see that on her chart.

01:06:05.962 --> 01:06:07.964
No, she's not.

01:06:08.965 --> 01:06:10.549
She's my boyfriend's mother.

01:06:10.633 --> 01:06:11.926
I see.

01:06:12.009 --> 01:06:13.052
So her son is…

01:06:13.135 --> 01:06:14.095
Yes.

01:06:14.178 --> 01:06:17.556
Goodness. He seemed to be pretty shocked.

01:06:17.640 --> 01:06:20.142
Our resident did explain everything,

01:06:21.018 --> 01:06:22.812
but you should tell him again.

01:06:22.895 --> 01:06:24.563
I will. Thank you.

01:06:33.239 --> 01:06:34.115
Professor.

01:06:34.198 --> 01:06:35.199
Yes?

01:06:35.282 --> 01:06:37.493
Mr. Ku Pil-jong's
CT angiography results came back.

01:06:37.576 --> 01:06:39.078
It's an MCA aneurysm rupture.

01:06:39.578 --> 01:06:41.080
Arrange an OR and prep for clipping.

01:06:41.163 --> 01:06:41.998
Yes, sir.

01:06:44.375 --> 01:06:47.420
The CT showed no signs
of brain damage or bleeding.

01:06:47.503 --> 01:06:48.546
Her skull is fine too.

01:06:49.088 --> 01:06:50.548
So she wasn't hurt too bad?

01:06:51.298 --> 01:06:53.050
There's no problem with her brain, right?

01:06:53.134 --> 01:06:55.302
No. As of now, everything's fine.

01:06:56.387 --> 01:06:57.263
That's a relief.

01:06:58.389 --> 01:06:59.223
Thanks.

01:06:59.974 --> 01:07:01.183
Thank you so much, Nam-kyung.

01:07:01.267 --> 01:07:02.727
It could've been worse.

01:07:03.728 --> 01:07:05.312
You must have been so shocked.

01:07:07.064 --> 01:07:07.940
Yeah.

01:07:12.737 --> 01:07:15.781
Are you still mad at me?

01:07:16.907 --> 01:07:18.325
How could I be mad?

01:07:19.535 --> 01:07:20.661
It's over now.

01:07:23.372 --> 01:07:24.790
I'm sorry for ghosting you.

01:07:25.541 --> 01:07:27.126
I was afraid if I replied to your text,

01:07:27.710 --> 01:07:28.794
I'd end up calling you,

01:07:29.962 --> 01:07:32.131
and then we'd meet up again.

01:07:32.214 --> 01:07:34.967
Hey, why are you being like this
over just a fight?

01:07:36.510 --> 01:07:38.137
We broke up, Nam-kyung.

01:07:39.430 --> 01:07:40.556
I told you.

01:07:42.349 --> 01:07:45.311
The next time you asked to break up,
that really would be it.

01:07:45.394 --> 01:07:47.938
No, I just said that out of anger…

01:07:53.569 --> 01:07:54.653
You know,

01:07:56.572 --> 01:07:57.656
being someone

01:07:58.324 --> 01:08:01.077
you could threaten
to break up with out of anger

01:08:03.120 --> 01:08:04.121
made me really sad.

01:08:05.748 --> 01:08:06.874
But I endured it.

01:08:08.918 --> 01:08:10.419
Because that's how much I liked you.

01:08:11.921 --> 01:08:12.797
Gi-dong.

01:08:15.132 --> 01:08:16.467
When we were fighting

01:08:17.093 --> 01:08:20.012
and not contacting each other,
I knew you went on blind dates.

01:08:20.096 --> 01:08:22.681
I also knew you were embarrassed
to tell your friends

01:08:22.765 --> 01:08:24.266
that I was looking for work.

01:08:25.476 --> 01:08:26.852
But I just pretended not to know.

01:08:29.021 --> 01:08:31.107
Because I thought I wasn't good enough.

01:08:33.442 --> 01:08:34.443
But this time,

01:08:36.070 --> 01:08:37.613
when you asked to break up,

01:08:38.447 --> 01:08:40.574
it was the first time I didn't feel sad.

01:08:40.658 --> 01:08:41.909
I felt relieved.

01:08:43.494 --> 01:08:45.871
Because I could hate you
instead of myself.

01:08:48.791 --> 01:08:49.959
But even after that,

01:08:51.210 --> 01:08:53.504
I still called you.

01:08:54.380 --> 01:08:55.840
When my mother fell,

01:08:56.423 --> 01:08:57.675
my mind just went blank.

01:08:58.759 --> 01:08:59.927
And I only thought of you.

01:09:00.845 --> 01:09:02.179
You're the only doctor I know.

01:09:04.390 --> 01:09:05.808
I know I shouldn't have called you.

01:09:07.059 --> 01:09:07.893
I'm sorry.

01:09:12.148 --> 01:09:13.065
I won't call again.

01:09:15.985 --> 01:09:17.069
Thanks for today.

01:09:21.866 --> 01:09:22.867
Hey, Hong Gi-dong.

01:09:26.453 --> 01:09:29.165
Call me. Just call.

01:09:30.332 --> 01:09:31.167
No.

01:09:32.001 --> 01:09:33.169
Call me.

01:09:34.545 --> 01:09:36.255
If you need to come to the hospital again,

01:09:36.755 --> 01:09:38.674
or if someone's sick or hurt,

01:09:38.757 --> 01:09:40.050
you can call me.

01:09:41.844 --> 01:09:42.678
Hey.

01:09:43.470 --> 01:09:44.972
We were together for seven years.

01:09:45.890 --> 01:09:49.018
Just because we broke up doesn't mean
you can't ask for a tiny favor.

01:09:53.480 --> 01:09:55.065
I won't ask to get back together again.

01:09:55.149 --> 01:09:56.734
I won't ask to be your friend either.

01:09:58.861 --> 01:10:01.405
So call me when you need to.

01:10:08.370 --> 01:10:10.748
You should go. Your mom must be waiting.

01:10:14.418 --> 01:10:15.252
Okay.

01:10:15.961 --> 01:10:16.962
I'll go on first then.

01:10:18.005 --> 01:10:18.839
Bye.

01:11:26.490 --> 01:11:27.658
What is it?

01:11:32.830 --> 01:11:33.664
Hey.

01:11:35.541 --> 01:11:36.417
Are you laughing?

01:11:38.168 --> 01:11:40.170
This is funny to you?

01:11:42.506 --> 01:11:43.507
I'm sorry.

01:11:55.185 --> 01:11:56.562
That was a close call.

01:11:57.438 --> 01:11:59.231
I've been in obstetrics forever.

01:11:59.315 --> 01:12:00.232
But emergency calls?

01:12:01.734 --> 01:12:03.152
I can never get used to them.

01:12:03.694 --> 01:12:05.529
How do you think we feel, Professor?

01:12:06.780 --> 01:12:07.865
Thanks, Do-won.

01:12:08.991 --> 01:12:10.826
You guys saved the baby.

01:12:13.412 --> 01:12:16.540
Is Dr. Oh okay?
Does she need medicine to calm her down?

01:12:17.333 --> 01:12:18.459
I'll check on her.

01:12:19.126 --> 01:12:19.960
Okay.

01:12:21.003 --> 01:12:22.588
But gosh,

01:12:22.671 --> 01:12:23.922
despite her attitude,

01:12:24.840 --> 01:12:25.799
she's good.

01:12:25.883 --> 01:12:28.218
And she's quick and fearless.

01:12:28.844 --> 01:12:29.720
You're right.

01:12:31.347 --> 01:12:32.181
Oh, right!

01:12:35.476 --> 01:12:36.602
Why are you here?

01:12:36.685 --> 01:12:39.063
You didn't oversleep
and miss your vacation too, did you?

01:12:39.146 --> 01:12:40.314
Someone else did that too?

01:12:40.397 --> 01:12:41.565
Me. Last year.

01:12:45.277 --> 01:12:46.111
Still,

01:12:46.195 --> 01:12:49.823
that breech C-section
you did last time helped, right?

01:12:49.907 --> 01:12:51.658
That wasn't me.

01:12:53.869 --> 01:12:55.079
It was my first time today.

01:12:56.080 --> 01:12:56.955
Really?

01:12:59.291 --> 01:13:01.919
Do-won, you've really grown!

01:13:02.002 --> 01:13:03.837
I wonder who trained you this well.

01:13:04.463 --> 01:13:06.215
Who? It wasn't me.

01:13:06.298 --> 01:13:07.966
-No…
-Did you do it all by yourself?

01:13:08.050 --> 01:13:10.094
I almost cried when we opened her up,

01:13:10.177 --> 01:13:12.137
but so many were watching,
so I barely held it in.

01:13:13.180 --> 01:13:14.390
You were calmer than I was.

01:13:14.473 --> 01:13:15.307
Gosh.

01:13:17.267 --> 01:13:18.268
I had no idea.

01:13:21.688 --> 01:13:23.440
Hi, Dr. Myeong.

01:13:26.110 --> 01:13:28.487
Just make a J-shaped incision
around the myoma.

01:13:28.570 --> 01:13:30.030
You don't need me for that.

01:13:32.533 --> 01:13:33.367
I have to go.

01:13:34.159 --> 01:13:35.077
I'm coming now.

01:13:36.703 --> 01:13:37.538
Bye, Professor.

01:13:45.337 --> 01:13:46.797
Can you buy me a coffee?

01:14:34.136 --> 01:14:35.137
Drink this.

01:14:35.220 --> 01:14:36.847
You seemed very startled earlier.

01:14:44.062 --> 01:14:44.897
Thank you.

01:14:45.481 --> 01:14:46.607
Good work today.

01:14:47.900 --> 01:14:49.485
Thank you for today.

01:14:51.195 --> 01:14:52.446
I really appreciated it.

01:14:53.655 --> 01:14:54.531
Sure.

01:14:57.534 --> 01:14:58.368
Okay.

01:15:05.626 --> 01:15:07.002
It's raining. Aren't you going in?

01:15:08.962 --> 01:15:11.131
No, I'm meeting someone.

01:15:12.257 --> 01:15:13.842
I see. Good night then.

01:15:14.801 --> 01:15:16.053
Sorry about that.

01:15:17.387 --> 01:15:19.264
-Take this.
-No, I'm fine.

01:15:19.348 --> 01:15:21.975
Take it. You can just give it back later.

01:15:23.101 --> 01:15:24.102
Thank you.

01:15:28.941 --> 01:15:30.484
And when you do…

01:15:33.862 --> 01:15:35.239
want to have dinner together?

01:16:22.995 --> 01:16:26.623
THANKS TO SUNG YU-BEEN
FOR HIS SPECIAL APPEARANCE AS HONG GI-DONG

01:17:04.161 --> 01:17:06.204
THANKS TO OUR SPECIAL GUESTS,
KIM JUN-HAN &amp; KWAK SUN-YOUNG,

01:17:06.288 --> 01:17:07.706
OUR ETERNAL AHN CHI-HONG &amp; LEE IK-SUN

01:17:08.248 --> 01:17:11.376
RESIDENT PLAYBOOK

01:17:11.460 --> 01:17:12.419
It is tough.

01:17:13.045 --> 01:17:14.963
These days,
I'm smiling, but not on the inside.

01:17:15.672 --> 01:17:18.508
The one I like
much more than I appear to is…

01:17:18.592 --> 01:17:19.509
Aren't you getting in?

01:17:19.593 --> 01:17:21.595
We still had things to talk about.

01:17:21.678 --> 01:17:24.723
Hey, I was curious about something.

01:17:24.806 --> 01:17:26.892
Asking to have dinner means it's a date.

01:17:26.975 --> 01:17:28.352
-With who?
-I think it's a guy.

01:17:28.435 --> 01:17:29.269
He likes her.

01:17:29.811 --> 01:17:31.772
-Welcome, ma'am.
-Thank you.

01:17:31.855 --> 01:17:32.856
-Mom.
-What?

01:17:32.939 --> 01:17:34.691
Please don't talk about me, okay?

01:17:34.775 --> 01:17:35.734
Seriously, don't.

01:17:36.360 --> 01:17:39.404
Wherever the dumplings went got a ton
of fun facts about Nam-kyung too.

01:17:39.488 --> 01:17:40.947
-Just eat one before you go.
-Mom!

01:17:41.990 --> 01:17:43.950
Couldn't the first-years come early?

01:17:44.034 --> 01:17:46.078
We're lucky they show up at all.

01:17:47.120 --> 01:17:49.373
Hey, what's wrong?
Hey, over here! Come here now!

01:17:49.456 --> 01:17:51.249
Hey, Sa-bi!

01:17:51.333 --> 01:17:52.292
Is it bad?

01:17:53.251 --> 01:17:54.503
It's not malignant, right?

01:17:55.087 --> 01:17:55.962
I…

01:17:56.838 --> 01:17:58.548
want to go back.

01:18:04.346 --> 01:18:06.348
Subtitle translation by: Jamie Jin
